==Problem description==
This article is aimed for a not turning on MacBook Air A1466 that has a corroded/damaged JTAG connector
==Symptoms==

*Not turning on
[[File:Screenshot JTAG Can spec of green dust kill a Macbook .png|thumb|Corroded JTAG connector (Figure 1)]]

==Solution==
JTAG connector (even if unused) that is corroded or damaged can cause several problems or help you figure out the problem. '''Connector must be replaced/removed and the area must be cleaned.'''

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ECWJ3Um1UQU Example video (youtube)].

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HlQ-FUMcNy0 Example video] where three A1466 MacBook Air machines did not have a green light on the charger caused by corroded JTAG connectors.

[https://youtu.be/O0_0YtdwgF0?t=2290 Good method for removal of JTAG connector]

You can buy them from [https://store.rossmanngroup.com/jtag.html here]